# A playing card
// A card says what its rank, suit and color are:  a deck, a pile or the game only reads them.
// It's a two sided view:  face up it shows its picture, face down the back every card shares.
// On the page each card is its own element, `<solitaire-card>`.

a "card" is a two sided view:
	// Ace is low:  ace = 1 ... king = 13
	- group "rank"
	- its "rank" is one of ace, 2 ... 10, jack, queen, king
		- it "is a (rank)"
	- its "value" is the position of its rank
	- it "is a face card" if its rank is jack, queen or king
	- it "is a number card" if it is not a face card

	- group "suit"
	- its "suit" is one of clubs, diamonds, hearts or spades
		- it "is a (suit)"
	- its "color" is one of red, black:
		red if it is a diamond or it is a heart
		black otherwise
	- its "symbol" is:
		"♣" if it is a club
		"♦" if it is a diamond
		"♥" if it is a heart
		"♠" otherwise

	// What a person, a test or the console calls it
	- group "names"
	- its "name" is its rank + " of " + its suit
	- it "is the (rank) of (suit)"
	// Its short name:  Q♠↓ is the queen of spades, face down
	- its "state" is:
		rank is 10 if its value is 10 otherwise the first letter of its rank as uppercase
		direction is "↑" if it is face up otherwise "↓"
		return rank + its symbol + direction

	// A drag puts it where it's dropped, if its pile's rules let it go;  what a click does is the game's
	- group "playing"
	- it can be dragged

	// One letter of unicode's Playing Cards, at the size of the text around it:  its pile scales it to fit -- styles.css
	- group "drawing"
	// Its face:  https://www.compart.com/en/unicode/block/U+1F0A0
	- its "picture" is:
		set column to its value
		if it is a club
			return item column of ["🃑", "🃒", "🃓", "🃔", "🃕", "🃖", "🃗", "🃘", "🃙", "🃚", "🃛", "🃝", "🃞"]
		if it is a diamond
			return item column of ["🃁", "🃂", "🃃", "🃄", "🃅", "🃆", "🃇", "🃈", "🃉", "🃊", "🃋", "🃍", "🃎"]
		if it is a heart
			return item column of ["🂱", "🂲", "🂳", "🂴", "🂵", "🂶", "🂷", "🂸", "🂹", "🂺", "🂻", "🂽", "🂾"]
		return item column of ["🂡", "🂢", "🂣", "🂤", "🂥", "🂦", "🂧", "🂨", "🂩", "🂪", "🂫", "🂭", "🂮"]
	- to draw its front:
		<ui-text color={its color}>{its picture}</ui-text>
	- to draw its back:
		<ui-text color="blue">🂠</ui-text>

	- to test card setup:
		get a new card whose rank is queen, suit is spades and direction is down
		its name should be "queen of spades"
		its color should be black
		its value should be 12
		its state should be "Q♠↓"
		it is a face card should be yes
		it is a spade should be yes
		it is a club should be no
		it is a queen should be yes
		it is a 2 should be no
		it is the queen of spades should be yes
		it is the queen of clubs should be no
		its picture should be "🂭"

		turn it over
		it is face up should be yes
		its state should be "Q♠↑"

		set seven to a new card whose rank is 7 and suit is hearts
		seven is a number card should be yes
		the color of seven should be red
		the picture of seven should be "🂷"
		the picture of a new card whose rank is ace and suit is clubs should be "🃑"
		the picture of a new card whose rank is king and suit is diamonds should be "🃎"
